Make shaderbg good enough for a detailed background on a laptop:

- Render at the output's real resolution, through fractional-scale-v1 and viewporter.
  It used to render at the logical size and let the compositor scale that up.
- Add --bake, which draws the slow parts of a shader to textures every so often, so
  that a frame costs next to nothing however detailed the picture is.  It also adds
  per-frame vertex setup, and a leading #version in the shader is kept first.
- Give shaders the real clock as iEpoch, since iTime stops during suspend.
- Set iFrame with glUniform1f.  It's declared a float, so using it was a fatal GL error.
- Destroy a layer surface before its wl_surface.  The other way round is a protocol
  error on wlroots compositors, which ended the program when a display was unplugged.

